---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../utils/url";

const layers = [
  ["Domain model", "Classes for threshold policies, rules, ranges, configured actions and persistent event logs, connected through CMDBuild domains and lookup taxonomies."],
  ["Database logic", "PostgreSQL and PL/pgSQL functions and triggers for configuration checks, range integrity, automatic evaluation of MeterReading data and event lifecycle management."],
  ["Application dispatch", "A Waterway pipeline for dispatchable events, structured payload construction and routing configured actions to notifications or maintenance processes."],
  ["Interface and reporting", "Dedicated navigation, dynamic forms, dashboards and configuration reporting to make the module's setup and operational state understandable."],
];
const results = [
  "Invalid formulas, inactive-rule references and inconsistent or overlapping ranges were blocked during configuration validation.",
  "A matching reading opened a traceable event linked to its asset, policy and measurement context.",
  "Repeated readings updated the existing open event rather than producing duplicate active events.",
  "A return to normal conditions closed the event and updated its runtime state.",
  "Configured events could generate notifications and start maintenance-process instances through the integrated dispatch flow.",
];
const technologies = ["openMAINT", "CMDBuild", "PostgreSQL", "PL/pgSQL", "Java", "Groovy", "JavaScript", "Waterway"];
---
<BaseLayout title="Threshold-Based Maintenance for openMAINT | Riccardo Paravano" description="Case study of a threshold-based maintenance module developed for openMAINT and CMDBuild during Riccardo Paravano's internship at PAT Srl.">
  <article class="container page case-study">
    <a class="back" href={withBase("/projects/")}>← All projects</a>
    <header class="case-header">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Enterprise software · Internship and BSc thesis</p>
        <h1>Threshold-Based Maintenance for openMAINT</h1>
        <p class="lead">During my internship at PAT Srl, part of the Zucchetti Group, I worked on an integrated subsystem that evaluates technical asset readings against configurable thresholds and converts relevant conditions into traceable events, notifications and maintenance workflows.</p>
      </div>
      <aside aria-label="Project facts">
        <span>Context</span><strong>Internship and experimental BSc thesis</strong>
        <span>Platform</span><strong>openMAINT / CMDBuild</strong>
        <span>Core technologies</span><strong>PostgreSQL, PL/pgSQL, Java, Groovy, JavaScript, Waterway</strong>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">Problem</p>
      <h2>Turn measurements into traceable maintenance decisions.</h2>
      <p>A numeric reading becomes operationally useful when it is connected to an asset, a measurement type, a unit of measure, evaluation rules and the actions that should follow. The module treats thresholds as configurable domain objects rather than isolated comparisons. This supports multiple rules, Boolean policy expressions, traceable event states and configurable actions within the existing platform.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">System architecture</p>
      <h2>Four cooperating layers.</h2>
      <div class="layer-grid">
        {layers.map((layer, index) => <div class="layer"><span>0{index + 1}</span><h3>{layer[0]}</h3><p>{layer[1]}</p></div>)}
      </div>
      <div class="flow" aria-label="Simplified processing flow">
        <div>Meter readings</div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div>Policy and rule evaluation</div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div>Traceable event</div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div>Configured action</div>
      </div>
      <p class="diagram-note">Simplified functional flow; implementation details and event handling remain within the openMAINT / CMDBuild environment.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">My contribution</p><h2>From requirements to an integrated subsystem.</h2></div>
      <div>
        <p>I contributed to requirements analysis, relational database modelling, PostgreSQL implementation, backend and frontend development, integration with existing platform components and functional testing. The work combined Java and Groovy backend tasks with JavaScript interfaces and database-side logic in PL/pgSQL.</p>
        <p>The evaluation flow processes MeterReading data, identifies applicable policies and active rules, checks measurement type and unit compatibility, evaluates the configured conditions and opens, updates or closes the corresponding event. Events can then be passed to the configured dispatch mechanisms.</p>
        <p>The implementation follows a rule-based, threshold-driven approach. It is not a machine-learning model and does not claim to estimate failure probability using statistical prediction.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">Validation</p>
      <h2>Configuration, runtime and integration checks.</h2>
      <ul class="results">{results.map((result) => <li>{result}</li>)}</ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">Technology</p>
      <h2>Enterprise platform and development stack.</h2>
      <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Technologies used">{technologies.map((item) => <li class="tag">{item}</li>)}</ul>
    </section>

    <section class="outcome">
      <p class="eyebrow">Outcome and learning</p>
      <h2>A configurable foundation for condition-based maintenance.</h2>
      <p>The module brings configuration, evaluation, event traceability and dispatch into the existing enterprise platform. The project gave me practical experience with a larger software system, database-centred application logic, integration constraints and the importance of validating both configuration and runtime behaviour.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .case-study { max-width: 1120px; }
  .back { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 3rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 750; }
  .case-header { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.45fr) minmax(16rem, .55fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 6rem); align-items: end; padding-bottom: 5rem; }
  .case-header aside { display: grid; gap: .35rem; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 1rem; background: var(--surface); }
  .case-header aside span { margin-top: .8rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; }
  .case-header aside span:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .case-study section { padding: 4.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .case-study section > p:not(.eyebrow), .split div:last-child p, .outcome p { max-width: 76ch; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .layer-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .layer { padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 1rem; background: var(--surface); }
  .layer span { color: var(--accent); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 850; }
  .layer h3 { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .layer p { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .flow { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .7rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 1rem; background: var(--surface); }
  .flow div { padding: .65rem .85rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: .65rem; font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 750; text-align: center; }
  .flow span { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 900; }
  .diagram-note { margin-top: .75rem; font-size: .85rem !important; }
  .split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 6rem); }
  .results { display: grid; gap: .75rem; max-width: 78ch; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .results li { position: relative; padding: 1rem 1rem 1rem 2.8rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: .8rem; background: var(--surface); }
  .results li::before { position: absolute; left: 1rem; color: #5ee0a0; content: "✓"; font-weight: 900; }
  .outcome { padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem) !important; border: 1px solid var(--border) !important; border-radius: 1.4rem; background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(142,197,244,.1), var(--surface)); }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .case-header, .split, .layer-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .case-header { padding-bottom: 3rem; } }
</style>
